cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the version-specific Zenodo record when available; otherwise use this repository's citation metadata."
type: software
title: "Amarna Pedigree Analysis"
version: "1.0.0"
authors:
  - family-names: "Minzenmay"
    given-names: "Thomas"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-1730-4528"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mintho/amarna-pedigree-analysis"
url: "https://github.com/mintho/amarna-pedigree-analysis"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reproducible exact full-pedigree likelihood calculations for eight published
  nuclear STR loci from the Amarna royal mummies. The archive contains Python
  software, documented JSON inputs, numerical results and validation checks.
  Five unique scored structures are compared using a normalised
  dropout-and-background-error observation model, with founder-prior
  sensitivity and locus-omission tests. Historical names are interpretations
  of sampled pedigree positions, not genetic outputs. The software is MIT
  licensed; original documentation and protectable result presentations are
  CC BY 4.0. Third-party observations and reference-frequency data are excluded
  from these grants; see LICENSING.md for scope and source attribution.
keywords:
  - Amarna
  - pedigree likelihood
  - short tandem repeats
  - kinship inference
  - reproducible research
